<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: HORSE RACING-IRISH CHAMPION HURDLE RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-IRISH CHAMPION HURDLE RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the grade one Irish</p>
<p>Champion Hurdle run over two miles (3.2 km) at Leopardstown on</p>
<p>Sunday.</p>
<p>1. Cockney Lad  10-1 (ridden by Richard Hughes)</p>
<p>2. Theatreworld 13-8 favourite (Charlie Swan)</p>
<p> 3. Dardjini     25-1 (Paul Carberry)</p>
<p>Seven ran.</p>
<p>Distances: one length, two lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Dan Daly and trained by Noel Meade in</p>
<p>Country Meath, Ireland.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 34,000 Irish punts ($55,640)</p>
</text>
